Package: karma2d
Title: Two-Dimensional Kumaraswamy Autoregressive Moving Average Models
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Vitor Bernardo Silveira", "Pereira", , "vitorpereira3115@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Bruna G.", "Palm", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Co-author of the statistical methodology"),
    person("Fabio M.", "Bayer", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Co-author of the statistical methodology")
  )
Description: Conditional maximum likelihood estimation, simulation,
    prediction and residual-based anomaly detection for the two-dimensional
    Kumaraswamy autoregressive moving average (2-D KARMA) model for bounded
    image data, in which each pixel follows a Kumaraswamy distribution in
    the median parametrization and the median follows a spatial ARMA
    structure over a strongly causal neighbourhood. Provides the
    Kumaraswamy distribution in the median parametrization, the analytic
    score vector, the conditional expected and observed information,
    quantile residuals, control-chart anomaly detection with morphological
    post-processing, and image quality metrics.
